  "notes": "Fetched with WebFetch on 2026-10-13. store.playstation.com pages (latest, browse, deals, collections, subscriptions) are client-rendered: WebFetch returned only the global PlayStation.com header (Store/PS5/Games/PS Plus/Accessories/News/Support menus with the short store variant of each menu), the store sub-nav (Latest/Collections/Deals/Subscriptions/Browse) and the short legal footer, with no shelves, tiles, filters or headings. Homepage sections are therefore limited to what is verifiable (menus, sub-nav, region line) plus the GTA VI pre-order hero, pre-orders shelf and PS Plus promo documented in research/playstation-store.md; shelf titles of the live Latest page are unverified. web.archive.org is blocked for WebFetch and WebSearch returned nothing useful. Product, search, sign-in and checkout-drawer content comes from research/playstation-store.md (my.account.sony.com and checkout.playstation.com cannot be fetched). PlayStation.com pages (support, store support, refund request, cancellation policy, gift cards, PS Plus, PS5, PS5 games, accessories, about SIE, studios, legal, site map) were fetched and their headings are quoted. status.playstation.com, blog.playstation.com and direct.playstation.com were not fetched; they are local summary pages kept under a host-named path (same convention as the clone's existing /my.account.sony.com sign-in). The store is digital-only, so there is no store locator. Assortment (2026-10-13, reference mode): stores/playstation-store/shelf.js adds about 275 real PS5/PS4 games, editions, add-ons, in-game currency and PS Plus memberships plus 39 PlayStation Direct consoles and accessories (local price/rating snapshot, upcoming release dates cross-checked against pushsquare.com's 2026 PS5 release list); the Latest page shows a featured carousel and shelf rows (New releases, Pre-orders, Bestselling games, Autumn Sale, Free-to-play, Add-ons and in-game currency, Game Catalog, PS VR2, PS5 hardware) whose titles are modelled on the real store but not verified against the client-rendered page. PlayStation Direct console and accessory pages list the hardware with filters; Games & merchandise keeps an empty state. The GTA VI evidence rows are unchanged and kept separate. The search icon opens a form, so search is checked as a page item. The real header logo goes to www.playstation.com/en-us; the clone keeps it on the store home.",
